# S11: the S04 audit/provision scripts are pinned by SHA-256 over their exact bytes (e.g. Invoke-S04AuditProcedure.ps1 pins
# sentinel-provision-common.ps1). A checkout that rewrites line endings (Windows autocrlf, hosted runners) changes the bytes
# and the pin correctly fails closed. Pins found in the repository and in the owner's private manifests are over LF bytes,
# with ONE exception (see below). tests/sentinel/s11-pinned-script-bytes.test.ts enforces this.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
# Pinned in CRLF form by a private S04 provision-package manifest (verified 2026-11-19): keep its historical bytes.
scripts/Invoke-S04ProvisionPackage.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Pinned by LF hash inside scripts/Invoke-S04OwnerSessionArchiveAudit.ps1 and private manifests, but not covered by *.ps1.
scripts/sentinel-owner-session-audit.ts text eol=lf
scripts/sentinel-owner-auth-snapshot.ts text eol=lf
